From 3e352158f8250536dfc4726bc6d378f0e4a60054 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:17:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add experimental AOT C queries for fixed redstone topology

Generate C11 input/target evaluators with constant state offsets and
block-specific rules, then attach them to the existing CPU cache. Intern
identical relative query bodies while keeping all instance state and events
independent. Keep
scheduled ticks, notifications, state commits and time in the existing
runtime. Check complete query topology before attachment and retain explicit
fallback and edit invalidation behavior.

Add benchmark-c, test-c and MCS export-c workflows. Report AOT generation
and compilation separately from simulation/attachment time, and require
generated queries to execute without fallbacks in the benchmark.

This is the first code-generation stage, not a standalone compiled
simulator or CUDA backend. Regenerate models after changing the core.

Base: 3d9b82c1c6b1d091fccab463c2afcf2502a4aa7d (PR #59)

Validation:
- ./nob test-c: query equivalence across 228224 evaluations, exact ordered
  writes, pending events, mode/delay changes, backend switching, boundary
  fallbacks, topology mismatch, empty models and edit invalidation.
- build/redstone_scaling --quick --no-output: all six reference/CPU
  scenarios pass with zero fallbacks.
- ./nob benchmark-c --quick --no-output: all six reference/generated-C
  scenarios pass with zero fallbacks and generated queries executed.
- Generated MCS model compiles, links and executes via sim_use_c.
- AddressSanitizer/UBSan on the new evaluator/attachment code and generated
  test functions; leak detection disabled because the sandbox lacks /proc.
